{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"RicardoCabral.icuvisor","latestVersion":"1.10.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"MCP server connecting intervals.icu training data to AI assistants.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral/icuvisor/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"MCP server connecting intervals.icu training data to AI assistants.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral/icuvisor/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"icuvisor is a local-first Model Context Protocol server that connects intervals.icu training data to AI assistants such as Claude, ChatGPT, Pi, Cursor, and other MCP-compatible clients.","moniker":"icuvisor","name":"icuvisor","packageUrl":"https://icuvisor.app/","publisher":"Ricardo Niederberger Cabral","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral/icuvisor/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral","releaseNotes":"### Added\n\n• The public core server supports opt-in `ServerOptions.StaticCatalog` for catalogs that remain fixed during each server's lifetime. It disables tool, prompt, and resource list-change notifications so unsupported subscription requests acknowledge no active notifications and finish promptly; existing server defaults remain unchanged.\n• Exposed independent opt-in stateless HTTP and JSON POST responses through CLI flags, environment variables, and JSON config. Defaults retain sessions and SSE responses; stateless HTTP is rejected when coach mode is enabled because athlete selection requires sessions.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral/icuvisor/releases/tag/v1.10.0","tags":["ai","coaching-tool","fitness","health","intervals-icu","llm","llm-integration","macos","mcp","mcp-server","wellness","windows"]}},"longDescription":"icuvisor is a local-first Model Context Protocol server that connects intervals.icu training data to AI assistants such as Claude, ChatGPT, Pi, Cursor, and other MCP-compatible clients.","moniker":"icuvisor","name":"icuvisor","packageUrl":"https://icuvisor.app/","publisher":"Ricardo Niederberger Cabral","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral/icuvisor/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral","releaseNotes":"### Added\n\n• The public core server supports opt-in `ServerOptions.StaticCatalog` for catalogs that remain fixed during each server's lifetime. It disables tool, prompt, and resource list-change notifications so unsupported subscription requests acknowledge no active notifications and finish promptly; existing server defaults remain unchanged.\n• Exposed independent opt-in stateless HTTP and JSON POST responses through CLI flags, environment variables, and JSON config. Defaults retain sessions and SSE responses; stateless HTTP is rejected when coach mode is enabled because athlete selection requires sessions.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/ricardocabral/icuvisor/releases/tag/v1.10.0","tags":["ai","coaching-tool","fitness","health","intervals-icu","llm","llm-integration","macos","mcp","mcp-server","wellness","windows"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.10.0/app.json","detailSha256":"0093e3c035c75ec3cc39748a3a624c27185580ed630366e5c96c9f0cd85641e3","releaseDate":"2026-11-06","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.10.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.8.0/app.json","detailSha256":"e4b76a8e9bcac944422e81870063aeb2084abc06b440761eeffb0fbc296ada66","releaseDate":"2026-10-13","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.8.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.6.5/app.json","detailSha256":"a7dc9a98cc0b7657897358e587208caf7fd515a5cbf30cbc9312c5ff20d3f0de","releaseDate":"2026-09-27","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.6.5"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.6.4/app.json","detailSha256":"dbead15ea68083e